      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A correction is a fall of about ten percent from the peak.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-correction",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · stock market correction"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Here's the reassuring part. Every single US market crash has eventually recovered to new highs.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "big": "100%",
          "label": "of crashes recovered, so far",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A crash is a sudden, steep drop across the whole market.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-crash",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · stock market crash"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The only variable is time. The deeper the fall, the longer the climb back.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Deeper = longer",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "chartDown"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The two thousand eight crash took years to fully recover.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-recession",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · Great Recession"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The pattern is oddly comforting. Every crash so far has eventually proven temporary.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "So far, temporary",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "clock"
          ]
